commit 77f4e0319afcbb988acdadd8150d819283a69f4a
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 20:45:18 2026 +0400

    Drop the attention mask from text-only VLM prompts (#700)
    
    * Drop the attention mask from text-only VLM prompts
    
    FastVLM, Gemma 3, Gemma 4 (both processors), Mistral 3 and SmolVLM
    paired every prompt with an all-ones attention mask, including prompts
    with no media. `ChatSession` reads any mask as a reason not to resume a
    cache (`carriesAttentionMask`), so on these models every text turn and
    every tool follow-up prefilled the whole conversation again.
    
    A text-only prompt is one unpadded sequence, so the mask carries
    nothing, and none of these models reads it without media. Their
    text-only prompts now carry no mask, as Qwen2-VL, Qwen3-VL, GLM-OCR,
    LFM2-VL and Muse-Glimmer already do. Prompts with media are unchanged.
    
    Measured on gemma-4-12B-it-4bit (Gemma4UnifiedProcessor), one tool call
    and two follow-up turns: the passes after the first reused 175, 226 and
    267 cached positions instead of 0, and their prompt time fell from
    3.1-3.9 s to about 1.0 s.

