commit f3da8683e4ad64f19e18831b7297196384d48b20
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 18:37:26 2026 +0200

    Report the reused cache prefix before prefill (#644)
    
    `PrefillParameters.progress` counts only the positions a prefill adds, so
    an application tracking how full a KV cache is cannot follow a prompt that
    resumes on a reused prefix -- as `ChatSession` arranges between turns, and
    as a template that re-renders the cached tail (Qwen 3 dropping the
    reasoning of past turns) forces it to rewind. The prefix is otherwise
    knowable only from the turn's `GenerateCompletionInfo.cachedPromptTokenCount`,
    once the turn has ended.
    
    Report it up front instead:
    
    - `PrefillParameters.prefix` is called once, before the first prefill
      forward, with the positions the cache already holds -- `0` when cold. It
      is the figure the same turn's completion info confirms.
    - Each token iterator reports it from its own cache progress, so the value
      is the cache's rather than a re-derivation: `TokenIterator`,
      `SpeculativeTokenIterator` and `MTPSpeculativeTokenIterator` each report
      the main cache once, and a draft prefill reports nothing.
    
    `prefix + processed` is what the cache holds while a prompt is prefilled,
    which is what a context gauge needs to stay correct mid-turn. Positions are
    the units `progress` already reports, so merged embedding positions on VLM
    turns count the same way in both.
    
    No model changes: models keep reporting through `progress`, and the new
    callback is optional, so existing call sites are untouched.

