commit 7a9b7e66fe839d248a2fc00e244dd04ea1aa384d
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 22:59:57 2026 +0200

    Let a ChatSession fork its cache into a new conversation (#641)
    
    Add `ChatSession.fork(history:)` to reuse prefix KV caches across conversations
    
    Starting every `ChatSession` with an empty cache causes expensive, redundant
    prefills for shared prompts (e.g. system instructions, tool schemas).
    `fork(history:)` creates a new session sharing the existing session's cache,
    configuration, and draft model, prefilling only the diff.
    
    Key changes:
    - `ChatSession.fork(history:)`: Returns a session with a sliced copy of the KV
      and draft caches; shares memory until write.
    - Cache pre-flight checks: Validates media presence before copying to avoid
      wasteful deep copies (e.g., in `VarianceNormalizedKVCache`).
    - Transcript validation: Requires exact token-by-token prefix matches and
      falls back to an empty cache if media is present.
    - Cache support: Implemented `copy()` for `TurboQuantKVCache`.
    - Concurrency: Made `fork` `nonisolated(nonsending)` so caller actors can fork
      without hop/executor overhead.

