commit c408452839dd5f42d59b1c5c7e8c2d100b9e0b97
Author: baozzz1 <42337806+baozzz1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 04:57:58 2026 +0800

    Fix the eps in the gated delta net q/k L2 norm (#633)
    
    Qwen3.5 and Qwen3-Next normalize q and k in the gated delta net with
    `invScale * rmsNorm(x, eps: 1e-6)`, where invScale = D^-0.5 and
    D = linear_key_head_dim. rmsNorm adds eps to mean(x^2), so the result
    is x / sqrt(sum(x^2) + D * 1e-6). The reference `l2norm` in
    transformers (qwen3_5 and qwen3_next) is x / sqrt(sum(x^2) + 1e-6),
    so the effective eps was D times too large (128x for
    Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B).
    
    Pass eps = 1e-6 / D to rmsNorm. Then
    sqrt(mean(x^2) + 1e-6 / D) = sqrt(sum(x^2) + 1e-6) / sqrt(D), which
    matches the reference. The invScale factors do not change.
    
    This affects the MLXLLM qwen3_5, qwen3_5_moe, qwen3_5_text and
    qwen3_next models and the MLXVLM qwen3_5 and qwen3_5_moe models.
    
    GatedDeltaQKNormTests compares each of the three layers with an output
    built from the same modules and the reference l2norm, on tokens scaled
    from 1 down to 1e-6. The largest per-token relative error goes from
    0.984 to 2.4e-6 or less.

